<title>BELGIUM: Brussels newcomer Systemat adds 3 pct.</title>
<headline>Brussels newcomer Systemat adds 3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Belgian hi-tech firm Systemat NV, an information technology services provider, rose three percent on Thursday supported by investor enthusiasm for newly listed companies.</p>
<p>By 1030 GMT the share was up 2.87 percent, or 40 francs, at 1,390 francs.</p>
<p>The share has risen 6.5 percent since it began trading on the Brussels bourse on Wednesday and is now worth 15.5 percent more than its issue price of 1,175 francs.</p>
<p>Systemat offers computer hardware, configuration, assembly, installation, training and support services.</p>
